    {
      "id": "6000000d-0000-4000-8000-00000000000d",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -200,
        -60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 2220,
        "height": 160,
        "content": "## Upsert patient\nValidates phone (\\d{8,15}) and status (inquiry|booked|handed_off) before touching Sheets. Looks up the existing row by phone first (Always Output Data, so a first-time patient yields an empty placeholder, not a stopped branch) and merges it with the new input, so a field the caller omits keeps its prior value instead of being blanked — Google Sheets' Append or Update writes an empty string for any mapped column whose value is undefined, so only columns we actually computed a value for are ever sent. Cell Format is RAW so phone is written and matched as the literal string, never reformatted into a number. Either Sheets call failing routes to notify-team (tool_failure); team_notified is set only when that alert actually sent."
      }
    }
